Version 4.1
SHEET 1 900 640
WIRE -32 128 0 128
WIRE 0 128 60 128
WIRE 140 128 240 128
WIRE 240 128 272 128
WIRE 0 336 0 128
WIRE 0 448 0 416
WIRE 240 176 240 128
WIRE 240 272 240 240
FLAG 0 448 0
FLAG 240 272 0
FLAG -32 128 INPUT
FLAG 272 128 CAP
IOPIN 272 128 Out
SYMBOL voltage 0 320 R0
SYMATTR InstName VSTEP
SYMATTR Value PULSE(0 5 10u 1n 1n 20u 50u)
SYMBOL res 156 112 R90
WINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2
WINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2
SYMATTR InstName RTEST
SYMATTR Value 1k
SYMBOL cap 224 176 R0
SYMATTR InstName CUNKNOWN
SYMATTR Value 10n
TEXT 0 -144 Left 3 ;#90 RC time constant
TEXT 0 -80 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=74fz9iwZ_sM
TEXT 0 -32 Left 2 ;A fast edge charges the capacitor under test through Alan's 1 kohm series resistor. The time taken to\nreach 63 percent of the step is R times C, so C follows from C = t / R.
TEXT 480 96 Left 2 !.tran 0 100u 0 20n
TEXT 480 136 Left 2 !.save V(INPUT) V(CAP)
TEXT 480 192 Left 2 !.meas tran CAP_20U FIND V(CAP) AT=20u
TEXT 480 232 Left 2 !.meas tran T63 WHEN V(CAP)=3.16060 RISE=1
TEXT 480 272 Left 2 !.meas tran TAU PARAM T63-10u
TEXT 480 312 Left 2 !.meas tran C_FROM_TAU PARAM (T63-10u)/1k
TEXT 480 352 Left 2 !.meas tran T5DIV WHEN V(CAP)=3.125 RISE=1
TEXT 480 392 Left 2 !.meas tran C_FROM_5DIV PARAM (T5DIV-10u)/1k
TEXT 480 464 Left 2 ;T63 uses the exact 63.2 percent point.\nT5DIV uses Alan's bench shortcut: set the\nstep to 8 vertical divisions and read the\ntime to rise 5 of them, which is 62.5\npercent and close enough.
